      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As much as I am against the whole thing because VRChat is not worth handing over my official ID and creating a link to my internet persona... this wouldn't work for 2 reasons:\n\n1. As stated in their response to why they only allow one account to be validated... \"Reduced implementation, maintenance, and complexity\". They want to do the minimum they can get away with to have this going.\n\n2. This would defeat the purpose of the whole verification thing.\n\nThe only real way \"to protect the kids\" if that was the real goal here, would be to make verification mandatory on everyone and make a hard barrier between adults and minors (minors can't see adults and viceversa).\n\nThe currently proposed half assed implementation doesn't prevent unverified adults from interacting with kids (so predators conveniently enough don't have to surrender their official ID) and doesn't prevent predators creating rooms without verification that kids can join.\n\nSo making whitelists to circumvent verification makes it even more worthless than it already is.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-03T01:28:17.947Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If you already know someone is of age (like you know them personally for example) but hasn't verified with VRChat, there needs to be another way to give this person access around the age verification system. Many people are not going to be comfortable with uploading images of their government-issued ID's to a third party for verification.",
